CHAPTER VII
COMMUNITY PARTICIPATION
Article 17
The community can participate in prevention and handling efforts for women victims of violence through individuals or institutions.
Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) is implemented through: providing information and/or reporting any potential violence and incidents of violence that become known;
conducting prevention against the occurrence of acts of violence against women;
providing protection services to women who become victims of violence;
assisting in the process of repatriation, social rehabilitation, and social reintegration of women victims of acts of violence.

CHAPTER III
OBLIGATIONS OF REGIONAL GOVERNMENT
Article 4
Regional government in implementing protection of women from acts of violence has the following obligations: to formulate strategic plans for protection of women against acts of violence for the short, medium, and long term as an integrated part of the Regional Medium-Term Development Plan (RPJMD);
to prevent and handle in an integrated manner the occurrence of acts of violence against women;
to encourage the responsibility of police institutions, prosecutorial institutions, judicial institutions, non-governmental organizations, religious institutions, and the general public to conduct coordination and cooperation in carrying out prevention and handling of the occurrence of acts of violence against women;
to optimize the role and function of institutions within the regional government environment related to carrying out prevention and handling of protection of women from acts of violence;
to provide facilities and infrastructure;
to conduct guidance, supervision and evaluation.

Article 20
Regional governments are obligated to conduct guidance and supervision of the implementation of protection for women victims of violence.
Guidance as referred to in paragraph (1), includes: Guidelines and fulfillment standards;
Technical guidance and training;
Provision of facilities;
Monitoring;
Evaluation.
Guidance as referred to in paragraph (2), is intended to realize the protection of women from acts of violence in accordance with minimum service standards implemented by SKPD and the community.
SKPD as referred to in paragraph (3) is the Regional Work Unit within the Regional Government of Paser Regency that is related to the protection of women against acts of violence.

Article 8
Prevention as referred to in article 5 letter a, includes: collecting data and information about women victims of violence as well as laws and regulations;
conducting education about anti-violence values towards women;
socializing laws and regulations related to the implementation of protection for women victims of violence;
establishing and facilitating the implementation of integrated service institutions for women victims by involving community elements;
encouraging community awareness of the importance of protection for women victims of violence;
Increasing women's awareness of the importance of complying with ethics, religious norms and cultural norms in behavior.
Prevention as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out by the Regional Government of the Regency, police institutions, prosecutorial institutions, judicial institutions, non-governmental organizations, and the community in accordance with their duties, functions, and responsibilities.

Article 28
Sexual violence as referred to in Article 24 letter d, includes: forced sexual relations committed against women residing within the scope of the household or outside the household;
forced sexual relations against women within the scope of the household or outside the household with other persons for commercial purposes and/or specific purposes;

